{"name":"Exotica","hex":"#938586","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"exotica","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of exotic","curious, strange, unusual and exotic things."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A genre of American music from the 1950s, characterized by an evocative musical focus on the islands of the South Pacific."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exotica"}],"entries":[{"title":"Exotica","blocks":[{"text":"Exotica is a musical genre that was popular during the 1950s to mid-1960s with Americans who came of age during World War II. The term was coined by Simon \"Si\" Waronker of Liberty Records in reference to Martin Denny's 1957 album Exotica."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exotica"},{"title":"Exotica (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Exotica is a 1994 Canadian film written and directed by Atom Egoyan, and starring Bruce Greenwood, Mia Kirshner, Don McKellar, Arsinée Khanjian, and Elias Koteas. Set primarily in the fictional Exotica strip club in Toronto, the film concerns a father grieving over the loss of a child and his obsession with a young stripper. It was inspired by Egoyan's curiosity about the role strip clubs play in sex-obsessed societies. Exotica was filmed in Toronto in 1993."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d1/Exoticaposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exotica_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/18/Ritualofthesavage.jpg/250px-Ritualofthesavage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/18/Ritualofthesavage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/18/Ritualofthesavage.jpg/250px-Ritualofthesavage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Les Baxter's Ritual of the Savage (Le Sacre du Sauvage) is one of the definitive albums of the exotica genre.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARitualofthesavage.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Atom_Egoyan_Arsinee_Khanjian.jpg/500px-Atom_Egoyan_Arsinee_Khanjian.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Atom_Egoyan_Arsinee_Khanjian.jpg/500px-Atom_Egoyan_Arsinee_Khanjian.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Director Atom Egoyan focused on strip clubs as outlets for society's sexual obsessions, while his pregnant wife Arsinée Khanjian played Zoe.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAtom_Egoyan_Arsinee_Khanjian.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Bruce_Greenwood_at_the_39th_Emmy_Awards_cropped.jpg/330px-Bruce_Greenwood_at_the_39th_Emmy_Awards_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Bruce_Greenwood_at_the_39th_Emmy_Awards_cropped.jpg/330px-Bruce_Greenwood_at_the_39th_Emmy_Awards_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bruce Greenwood starred as Francis, having met Egoyan before the director became internationally prominent.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABruce_Greenwood_at_the_39th_Emmy_Awards_cropped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9d/Mia_Kirshner_red_lighted_cropped_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9d/Mia_Kirshner_red_lighted_cropped_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Canadian actress Mia Kirshner received positive reviews for her p